1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,000
Nobody under forty is finding
La Grotta tonight.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
It's not the food.
It's one line of Google text.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,200
Enzo and Maria have run
this room for years.

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,400
Fourth generation, same
building on Lygon Street.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,600
You can smell the pappardelle
before you sit down.

6
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,500
The regulars know which
table is theirs.

7
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:20,000
Then a Monday came with
four empty tables.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Enzo walked the floor.
The settings were fine.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The kitchen was ready. Maria
searched "Carlton Italian".

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
"We're not even on
the first page."

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
A newer place had forty-seven
photos and fresh reviews.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
The algorithm doesn't hold
grudges. It just forgets.

13
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,500
The street doesn't
turn against you.

14
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,500
It just stops
mentioning you.

15
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:38,000
Four tables.

16
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Four.

17
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
This room has fed the street for
a century — tonight it's a secret.

18
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
"I will not stand for it."

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
"I am sitting, but I
will not stand for it."

20
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Maria said: we choose to be found,
or we wait to be remembered.

21
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,200
She didn't hire anyone. She
updated the listing herself.

22
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,800
One line. Three photos.

23
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,200
I'm Bella — ciao for now.
